# Yuno-only — do not overwrite on Skipii merges

Yuno tracks **deciocrytek/Skipii** (`git remote upstream`) but is its own app. When bringing in upstream commits, **port Skipii fixes/features without reverting Yuno product/UI** unless the user explicitly says otherwise.

**Authoritative detail:** `docs/yuno-preserve-on-merge.md`.

## Never remake a Skipii feature

When a Skipii update adds or changes a feature, **port the upstream code** (`com.decio.skipii` → `com.yuno`, user-facing Skipii → Yuno). Do not write a new gesture, animation, layout, or screen that only “does the same thing.” Yuno chrome this file says to keep (glass nav, no PlayerBar, Settings page, portrait edge scrub, mini-player, Shorts rail) stays; the upstream behavior is wired into that chrome.

## Always keep (Yuno)

| Area | What to protect |
|------|-----------------|
| **Branding** | Name **Yuno**, `com.yuno`, launcher/wordmark — never ship Skipii/Castii/`com.skipii` user strings. |
| **Updates source** | APK checks/downloads **only** from **`danielkanan/Yuno`** (`GITHUB_RELEASES_REPO` / `BuildConfig`). Updater **code** may merge from upstream; release **origin** must stay Yuno. |
| **Colours / appearance** | System · Light · Dark only (`ThemeSettings.mode`). **No** wallpaper colours, named palettes, or theme chip rows. **Do** keep liquid-glass toggle in Settings. |
| **Settings UX** | Full **Settings page** (`Settings.kt`) — not Skipii’s old account-only settings sheet. No re-adding appearance colour chips. |
| **Liquid glass nav** | `LiquidGlass.kt`, `floatingtabbar/`, `GlassNav.kt`, glass in `NavBar.kt` — Yuno tab bar + lens motion. |
| **Player controls** | On-video overlay is **upstream `VideoView`** (`OverlayTile` / `OverlaySeek` / `OverlayPlay`, fullscreen cards, `pendingTap` so a double tap only seeks). Seek glyphs are upstream `seekIcon` (15/20/25 included) and follow Settings › Playback. Zoom scales the picture only; captions stay on the unzoomed box. **Portrait edge scrub** stays. **No** `PlayerBar.kt`. **No** Settings choice for “controls in the bar”. |
| **Mini-player** | Glass accessory row, `FadingLine` titles, morph docking (`PlayerUi.kt`, `PlayerMorph.kt`). |
| **Shell / motion** | Morph rules, collapsing headers, page vignettes, `SharedVideoTexture`, no ripples (`pressable`), status bar over video. |
| **Typography / truncation** | Yuno icons, weights, `Mass`. `FadingLine.kt` where Yuno uses fade — not `…` on those surfaces. |
| **Thumbnails** | `sharpenFeedThumbnail` + `UiKit.kt` `Thumbnail` styling. |
| **Shorts look** | Yuno glass rail stays. Drag-to-seek, the double-tap thumb burst, and the progress line are **upstream `Shorts.kt`** (`scrubTo` / `endScrub`, `shortTaps`, `ThumbBurst`, `Line*`), not a rewrite. |

## Your changes — ask only if an update touches them

When you change or add something in Yuno (a layout, a screen, a setting, a behavior), write it here **and** in `docs/yuno-preserve-on-merge.md` in the same turn, without being asked. One line: what changed, and where it lives. Do not file it under **Always keep** or **OK to follow upstream** until you decide.

On an upstream merge, ask only if that update **conflicts with or rewrites** one of these lines. Leave the others alone and do not ask about them. For each one Skipii actually changes, ask whether to **keep** it or **let Skipii replace it**.

- **Keep** — move the line under **Always keep**.
- **Let Skipii replace it** — drop the line and follow upstream for that spot.

- Loading skeletons (`Skeleton.kt`) on feeds, the channel page, and comments. Spinners stay for playback, sign-in, and posting.
- Settings has no developer card: no "Made by @…", "Come say hi", or social links (`Settings.kt`).
- Settings uses BitChord's settings chrome throughout (`Settings.kt`, `SettingsChrome.kt`, `IosSwitch.kt`, `PillSegmentedControl.kt`): floating top bar, their padding and grouped cards, the press-stretch switch, and the sliding segment pill. Yuno's own settings stay (playback, captions, SponsorBlock, Shorts, appearance as System/Light/Dark plus liquid glass, language, notifications, about, account). The settings page does not draw `PageTopFade`.
- Signed-out Home still shows recommendations (`InnerTube.guestHome` in `Account.kt`, chosen in `LibraryData` in `Feeds.kt`). Anonymous home browse is a sign-in wall, so guests search for popular videos.
- Home pull-to-refresh stretches the top bar (more top and bottom padding — about 6dp more at the reload point, and it still grows if you pull past while the wordmark size and fill stay put — wordmark grows to the right from the gutter, fades to 20% with a white left-to-right fill that finishes at the size limit, haptic when full, then the wordmark fills and empties starting fill-unfill-fill, then unfill-fill with a half-second hold between those, and after reload it finishes that pass through to a full fill before returning to normal with a click and a quick scale jump; a pull during that animation still grows the bar and clicks, and letting go of a pull that started during the reload does not start another one) via `BarPullRefresh.kt`, wired in `HomeScreen` (wordmark), `SubscriptionsScreen` and `LibraryScreen` (page titles), `PageTopBar`, `LargePageBrandMark`, and `LargePageTitle`. Playlist pages still use the circular indicator.

## Ask on each merge

- **Playback / extraction / deps:** `YouTube.kt`, `PlayerFallback.kt`, `PlaybackService.kt`, parsers, Gradle/Media3, ProGuard.
- **Shorts disk bank:** large `ShortsBank.kt` changes — confirm first.
- A line under **Your changes** only when this update conflicts with it or rewrites that spot.

## OK to follow upstream (unless it breaks “Always keep”)

- Audio-only stage / `VideoStage` behavior.
- Queue clear animation (`Sheets.kt`).
- SponsorBlock **settings UI** (service skip logic still ask with playback if non-trivial).
- Related list copy, RTL/layout policy, Playful.kt, Comments panel.
- Locale strings, parser fixes, new Skipii features that don’t replace rows above.
- Home category chips: upstream `HomeChips` → `UnderlineTabs` (underlined words). Not filled chips.
- Channel page, and Subscriptions: tapping a channel **opens the channel** (does not filter the feed underneath).
- Hold-on-video actions live in the iOS-style hold menu (`HeldMenu` / `VideoHeldMenu`), including Not interested and Don’t recommend channel. **No** long-press bottom sheet (`VideoOptionsSheet`).
- Settings › Playback shows skip distance, keep chapters open, picture-in-picture when you leave, zoom to fill, music at normal speed, remember speed, and audio only.
- Fullscreen pinch zoom to fill (and the Settings switch) actually scales the picture.

## Merge workflow

1. Read this rule + `docs/yuno-preserve-on-merge.md`. If this update conflicts with or rewrites a line under **Your changes**, ask before taking Skipii’s version of that spot.
2. `git merge upstream/main` (or tag); resolve **file-by-file**.
3. `rg -i "skipii|castii|com\\.skipii|PlayerBar" app/src` — investigate hits; confirm release repo still **Yuno**.
4. `./gradlew assembleDebug`; `testDebugUnitTest` if parsers changed.
5. **End-of-update review** (do this every merge, without being asked). Two numbered lists, numbers continuing:
   - **Left out** — user-visible Skipii changes not shipped in Yuno (on purpose or missed).
   - **Added** — user-visible Skipii changes that did land.
6. Wait for answers: `1. agree`, `2. disagree`, and so on.
   - **Left out + agree** — keep it out. If that protection is missing from this rule and `docs/yuno-preserve-on-merge.md`, add it under **Always keep**.
   - **Left out + disagree** — port that Skipii behavior into Yuno, then record it under **OK to follow upstream** (and remove any “always keep” line that blocks it).
   - **Added + agree** — keep it. Record it under **OK to follow upstream** if it is not already there. If it is only in code and not actually on screen, wire it before calling it added.
   - **Added + disagree** — take it back out and protect the Yuno behavior under **Always keep**.
7. After that pass, post a **fresh** numbered left-out / added list (what is true now, not the list just voted on). **Keep posting a new list after every fix pass until you say all is good.**
8. Summarize: upstream range, what changed in the rule, anything still waiting on an answer.

**Never commit or push** unless you ask.
